# Phase 18 factory null client-array slot parity

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 10:12:20 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Implementation revision: `1b1d4e2a`
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1, `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`
- Scope: `MQClientAPIFactory.onNameServerAddressChange` behavior when the public client array contains null

## Finding and change

Pinned Java iterates the mutable array returned by `getClients()` in index
order and invokes each client. A null slot raises `NullPointerException` when
reached, after earlier clients have already received the address update. A
null address still invokes earlier clients before encountering the same null
slot. Rust previously skipped null client slots. The factory now checks and
updates slots in order and returns `NullClient(index)` at the first missing
client, preserving prior slot updates.

The invoked Java factory fixture records the null-slot error for both a
non-null and null address, plus the address arrays after each partial failure.
The Core factory regression consumes those fields and restores the mutated
slot before continuing the existing change and shutdown checks.

